You have CRUD access to one flexible text buffer.

- `read_buffer` returns its contents, optionally over a line range, with line
  numbers.
- `write_buffer` sets the entire buffer only when it is empty.
- `edit_buffer` replaces one exact, uniquely matching substring.
- `clear_buffer` empties the buffer.

Prefer `edit_buffer` for incremental changes. Use `write_buffer` only after the
buffer has been cleared or when initializing an empty buffer.
